(std.math.decimal.decimal-rule std.math.decimal.numeral-digit) ; rule decimal: a numeral is written, and never guessed: every relation of the module is closed — std.math.decimal.numeral-digit is a rule of std.math.decimal
(std.math.decimal.decimal-rule std.math.decimal.numeral-prefix-digit) ; rule decimal: a numeral is written, and never guessed: every relation of the module is closed — std.math.decimal.numeral-prefix-digit is a rule of std.math.decimal
(std.math.decimal.decimal-rule std.math.decimal.numeral-prefix-named) ; rule decimal: a numeral is written, and never guessed: every relation of the module is closed — std.math.decimal.numeral-prefix-named is a rule of std.math.decimal
(std.math.decimal.decimal-rule std.math.decimal.numeral-prefix-zero) ; rule decimal: a numeral is written, and never guessed: every relation of the module is closed — std.math.decimal.numeral-prefix-zero is a rule of std.math.decimal
